    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are leaning heavily on speed and favorable matchups today, with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) leading the charge as our premier start. His matchup against Lowder provides the perfect storm: a 4.81 xERA starter, a friendly park environment, and crucially, a slow delivery that projects for a high-probability stolen base opportunity. **Christian Yelich** (74.33) and **Yordan Alvarez** (74.02) follow closely behind; while **Yordan Alvarez** faces a lefty, his elite 0.443 xwOBA overrides the platoon disadvantage, and **Christian Yelich** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and dynamic platoon leverage that keeps his ceiling high despite the risk of deGrom-level pitching volatility elsewhere.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Carson Benge** (33.04), who fell well short of our 40.0 efficiency floor. Despite some underlying potential, his matchup against the elite 2.95 xERA of S\u00e1nchez makes him a liability today, and the Optimizer correctly prioritized the reliable contact profiles of **Caleb Durbin** and **Chase Meidroth** even in suboptimal order slots. Caution is warranted at the corners, as **Kazuma Okamoto** (42.03) and **Josh Smith** (43.18) are facing deGrom. While they remain in the lineup, their scores are heavily suppressed by the SP\u2019s dominance; we are essentially hoping for a high-leverage mistake rather than sustained production. We will monitor **Lars Nootbaar** and **Trea Turner** closely at the top of the order, as their ability to generate Runs and SBs is vital to maintaining our Roto standing in the final stretch of the season.",
